# MediatR (`lib/MediatR`)

Custom CQRS dispatcher — **not** the Jimmy Bogard NuGet package.

## Flows

| Flow | API | Returns |
|------|-----|---------|
| Commands / queries | `IMediator.SendAsync` | `Result` / `Result<T>` |
| Notifications | `IMediator.PublishAsync` | nothing (0..N handlers) |

Pipeline: `ValidationBehavior` → `ExceptionBehavior` → handler.

## Registration

```csharp
services.AddMediatR(Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly());
```

Called from `Application.DependencyInjection` — scans Application assembly for handlers and validators.

## Handler contract (consumer apps)

Handlers live in **Application** only. See `application.mdc` for templates.

```csharp
public sealed record SignInRequest(...) : ICommand<SignInResponse>;

public sealed class SignInRequestHandler(UserRepository userRepo)
    : IRequestHandler<SignInRequest, SignInResponse>
{
    public async ValueTask<Result<SignInResponse>> HandleAsync(SignInRequest request, CancellationToken ct = default)
    {
        var result = new Result<SignInResponse>();
        // Execute / Handle Result
        return result;
    }
}
```

## Namespaces

```text
MediatR.Abstractions       IMediator, ICommand, IQuery, IRequestHandler
MediatR.Results            Result, Result<T>, Error, ErrorCode
MediatR.Behaviors          ValidationBehavior, ExceptionBehavior
MediatR.DependencyInjection AddMediatR
```

## Stays outside the lib

Repositories, EF, entities, feature DTOs, AI, Blazor — Application/WebApp consume `IMediator` only.

Version roadmap: `lib/MediatR/README.md`.
